cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ClaimCheck: A Dependency-Confusion Exposure Checker for Internal Packages"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Choksi"
    given-names: "Krishita Sanjay"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Krishita17/claimcheck"
abstract: >-
  ClaimCheck is a defensive, read-only exposure-assessment tool that reads an
  organization's internal dependency names from manifests, lockfiles,
  registry-scope configs, CI files, and Dockerfiles, then checks each name
  against the public PyPI and npm registries to determine whether an attacker
  could claim it (dependency confusion). It produces a prioritized,
  fallback-aware exposure report with a concrete remediation action per name.
keywords:
  - dependency-confusion
  - supply-chain-security
  - software-supply-chain
  - pypi
  - npm
  - sca
  - devsecops
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-03"
